    <td valign="top"> 
      <p align="center" class="Heading">FAQ</p>
      <p align="center" class="sub-head">Level Restrictions<br>
        <span class="longtext"> We have no level limits. Since no one can get 
        an invite until they have worked with current members, their primary character 
        levels will match those of current members.<br>
        <br>
        As for alts, once you are a member of the guild, all of your alts are 
        welcome as well, no matter the level. We are trying to promote a family 
        atmosphere here and the more people can be in touch, the better.<br>
        </span> </p>
      <p align="center" class="sub-head">Accessing the Board<br>
        <span class="longtext">The board can be found here:&nbsp; <a href="http://pub41.ezboard.com/bhouseofbastards">Message 
        Board</a>&nbsp;<br>
        You must register to begin posting on the board.&nbsp; Guild members should 
        post a single message to the message board requesting access.&nbsp; A 
        moderator will grant them access.&nbsp; Guild members should immediately 
        post all of their characters to the roster section and keep that up to 
        date.</span></p>
      <p><span class="sub-head">Guild Alliances</span><br>
        <span class="longtext">Still working on these.&nbsp; But, The Golden Order 
        are becoming fast friends.</span></p>
      <p><span class="sub-head">How the The Vault Works</span><br>
        <font face="Verdana,Arial" size="2"><span class="longtext">The treasurer 
        is in charge of the vault and the guild funds.<br>
        <br>
        The vault is a storage facility for research items, cash, magic items, 
        items used in skills advancement and tradable quest items. The idea behind 
        the vault is a sort of &quot;club&quot; that we all contribute a little 
        to here and there but we all benefit from. The treasurer will use items 
        in the vault and the vault funds to buy and sell in the bazaar to increase 
        the overall wealth of the vault.<br>
        <br>
        You will never be required to donate to the vault (with exceptions noted 
        below).<br>
        <br>
        All items and coin donated to the vault become guild property to be used 
        and spent at the treasurers discretion.<br>
        <br>
        You may take a loan from the vault, again at the treasurers discretion.<br>
        <br>
        Money in the vault can be used for skill advancement, again at the treasurers 
        discretion. Note: If you get money to advance a skill from the vault, 
        it will be expected that you will donate back a percentage of the profits 
        you gain from using that skill to the vault. The amount of that donation 
        will be up to you.<br>
        <br>
        Items in the vault can be purchased from the vault at a discount from 
        what it is normally available on the market. The treasurer will decide 
        the sale price if sold to a guild member.<br>
        <br>
        Requests can be made to the vault. i.e. I need a Ghoulbane, can you see 
        if you can get me one? Again the treasurer will attempt to fulfill these 
        requests as funding and opportunity arises. Note: Requests made to the 
        vault must be purchased in cash or trade items. No loans will be issued 
        for requests.<br>
        <br>
        All research items, gems and trade skill materials gained during guild 
        raids will be donated to the vault. These may be removed from the vault 
        at any time, free of charge. Exception being items of a 50plat or greater 
        value will need to be purchased from the vault. If research items are 
        used and they create spells that are not needed by the researcher, those 
        spells will be given back to the vault for storage or resale.<br>
        <br>
        If, during a raid, you are awarded a magic item and it replaces an item 
        you currently own, the item it replaces will automatically be donated 
        to the vault.<br>
        <br>
        The vault may have a collection of wisdom and intelligence gear that may 
        be borrowed for trade skill studies.<br>
        <br>
        If you are out on your own, or even with a bunch of guild members on a 
        non scheduled raid, it is entirely up to you if you contribute to the 
        vault at all.<br>
        <br>
        If you are on a raid and want your share of the loot donated to the vault, 
        of course this is an option, but is never required.<br>
        <br>
        Any magical items looted during a raid that no one on the raid can use 
        can be donated to the vault if all members of the raiding party agree. 
        Otherwise, the vault may also buy it, at the treasurers discretion and 
        at a agreed upon rate below normal trade value, or the vault can be asked 
        to sell it, with the vault getting a pre agreed upon percentage or flat 
        fee for the sale. Otherwise, individual raid members can sell it independently 
        and split the money with the raiding party, as we have done in the past.<br>
        <br>
        Again, the idea is a sort of club. If everyone contributes a little to 
        it, it will grow into something of great benefit to everyone. Again, we 
        don't want to twink our characters but we can provide a healthy support 
        system where we can take advantage of the fact that we are an organized 
        group and there is always power in numbers.</span></font></p>
      <p align="left" class="sub-head">Officers<br>
        <span class="longtext"> Ziff Harbinger - Guild Leader<br>
        Wildride - Officer<br>
        Luifang - Officer</span></p>
      <p><span class="sub-head">Leaving and Rejoining the Guild</span><br>
        <span class="highlighted">Still in discussion. </span> </p>
      <p><span class="sub-head">General Do's and Don'ts</span><br>
        <br>
        <span class="longtext">These are not so much things that would be considered 
        punishable offenses, but common behaviors we recommend and encourage others 
        to follow.<br>
        <br>
        Again, this is not a &quot;complete&quot; list. In fact, this set of guidelines 
        is probably expected to be a living document that will forever be changing 
        and growing.</span></p>
      <p align="left"><span class="sub-head"> General</span><br>
        <span class="longtext">Dude Speak is not permitted. Anachronisms, common 
        vernacular and roleplaying are encouraged. However, Dude speak is not 
        any of those things and is an inappropriate representation of the guild.</span></p>
      <p><span class="sub-head">Raids</span><br>
        <span class="longtext">During guild raids and events the raid leaders 
        will assign looters. Only the looters should loot corpses unless otherwise 
        instructed by the raid leader. Should the designated looter by AFK or 
        LD a new one will be temporarily assigned.<br>
        <br>
        How loot is divided for a Raid is decided by the Raid leader. In the event 
        the Raid leader is AFK or LD, guild leaders and officers will determine 
        the division of loot.<br>
        <br>
        It is important that you listen and are fully cooperative at all times 
        during a raid. If someone has a designated responsibility you should follow 
        their instructions and make no attempt to override or interfere with instructions. 
        This includes things like staying in the fight until the designated &quot;RUN&quot; 
        caller declares it is time to run. It also includes staying put until 
        the puller gives the &quot;OK&quot; to move. There are many detailed aspects 
        of a well planned raid and it is important that you understand what role 
        you play and what roles everyone else plays. It is important that you 
        follow the instructions of those assigned duties and responsibilities 
        and do not interfere with them. Failure to do so will often result in 
        the deaths of multiple party members.</span><br>
      </p>
      <span class="sub-head">Rules and Enforcement</span><br>
      <ol>
        <li><span class="longtext">Violation of any portion of the charter.</span><span class="longtext"><br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Using excessive profanity in guild chat.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Using profanity or sexually explicit terms, 
          in public message systems within EQ (Tells, Shouts, Says, Auctions etc.) 
          or a message board such as the Cazic-Thule Corner.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Engaging in a verbal attacks, threats or otherwise 
          harassing another person in game or on the message board.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Abuse or misuse of Guild funds or items.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Purposely kill stealing or ninja looting.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Begging. Begging is the act of asking favors, 
          including but not limited to money, equipment, buffs, teleports and 
          resurrections, without making a reasonable offer of compensation. As 
          a guild member, we will often do favors for other members and ask nothing 
          in return, but should you ask for that favor it will always be expected 
          that you will offer something in return. Weather or not the person doing 
          the favor accepts the compensation is entirely up to them.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Going anonymous. No guild member should go 
          anonymous. If you feel it is necessary to hide your class or race, please 
          use the /Roleplay command. If you feel you need to hide your guild tag 
          then you should either seriously consider why you are in Dusk Eternal 
          or seriously consider the actions you are about to take.<br>
          </span></li>
        <li><span class="longtext">Responding to threads on CTC or any other message 
          boards or that contain flames about Dusk Eternal or any of it's factions. 
          In the event of excessive flames or abuses directed at the Guild, please 
          inform an officer and it will be handled appropriately.</span><br>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="highlighted">&nbsp;</p>
      <p><font size="2" class="longtext">First offense - Warning #1 - These are 
        assigned to the individuals over-all account and thus applicable to any 
        character the user plays.<br>
        <br>
        Second Offense - Warning #2 - These are also assigned to the individuals 
        account and apply to all characters played. After a second warning is 
        issued, the player will not be allowed to guild additional alts for 1 
        month.<br>
        <br>
        Third Offense - The Character in violation is removed from the guild. 
        Alts are allowed to stay in the guild. After a third warning, the player 
        may not add alts to the guild for 6 months.<br>
        <br>
        Additional Offenses - Removal of other characters and potentially (if 
        all officers are in agreement) complete removal from the guild.<br>
        <br>
        Any officer can issue a warning to any character at any time. Full details 
        of why the warning was assigned to the player will need to be posted in 
        the officers forum. Should the other two officers feel the warning is 
        unwarranted, it can be removed. However, this will be an EXTREMELY rare 
        case. The guild leader is the only person who can issue a warning to an 
        officer. The officers, if in agreement with each other, can issue a warning 
        to the guild leader. Once a warning has been assigned to a player, the 
        offending player will receive an e-mail explaining the exact details of 
        why the warning is being issued and the implications of that warning.<br>
        <br>
        Warnings will NOT be discussed with other players unless the player receiving 
        the warning requests it.<br>
        <br>
        Warnings last for 6 months. If no additional warnings are received during 
        a 6 month period then the warning is removed.<br>
        <br>
        There may be occasions where individuals would require immediate dismissal 
        from the guild. This is an extreme situation and should not be taken lightly. 
        Should this become necessary the individual will first be asked to log 
        out and to not log in a guild tagged EQ player for 24 hours while the 
        matter is being decided by the officers. If the player refuses to cooperate, 
        they will be temporarily removed from the guild to prevent further problems 
        being associated with the guild name until the matter is decided. The 
        officer in question should gather all of the information necessary and 
        post it to the officers forum and contact the officers. A vote on the 
        matter should be had immediately, weather that be via phone, web, e-mail 
        or otherwise. If all officers agree, the offending player will be removed 
        from the guild. A post will be placed in the members section explaining 
        in detail why the action was taken. Comments and suggestions from the 
        guild in general will be taken for 1 week. During this time the offending 
        player will still be allowed to post and defend themselves via the message 
        board. If after 1 week the officers see no need to change the ruling, 
        the player in question will be permanently removed from the guild and 
        all access to the message board be revoked. If compelling reasons can 
        be put forth that sway the officers to change the ruling, they will decide 
        the level and severity of the punishment.<br>
        <br>
        Removal from the guild due to warnings and violation is permanent. Players 
        removed in this manner will not be allowed reentry to the guild, ever.<br>
        <br>
        Additionally, The actions of one character, and one account will be considered 
        to be the actions of a single individual, regardless of how many people 
        play the characters on that account. Unless it can be proven that the 
        account was used by someone other than the original owner without their 
        permission, all actions taken by the characters on an account will be 
        considered to originate from the same source. For purposes of enforcement 
        and violations, no distinctions will be made between who is playing the 
        account at any given time. </font><br>
      </p>
